      "message": "PTAL\n\nApologies, the design has changed so much since when I first made this CL. After going through it, I realize that the majority of the last patchset is redundant. \n\nSince the buffer will be written and uploaded to by the StorageManager, there is no need to expose a separate write mapped storage function. This is because the storageManager will write directly with getMappedStorage. Furthermore, since there is only a single slot for uniiform storage buffers, there is no need to specify to the buffer manager which should be used.\n\nInstead, all we need to add is a way for rendersteps to specify where (if any) its storage buffer should be visible",
